# T6: TIMED arm C: c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-w1 ALONE (wave 1 without wave 2) in this image, on the same tests as the pair jobs (T1, T2, T4, T5, T7, T8), after its own all-four reset. It is the in-image reference for wave 2's increment: B (T2, T5, T8) against C (T3, T6) is what the multi-user SDPA launch and the conv-gates spread add to the same stack in the same window,
# which no earlier window measured together. Judge PAIRED per round against the NEIGHBOURING B run (T3 against T2, T6 against T5: the same position-keyed rounds, one job apart in time, not hours), never by unpaired medians; check the load average.
# READ: as the pair jobs (texts equal to the control's, per-seat rate at 32k and about 128k, the lever lines of wave 1); then the increment: C minus B per round at 32k, at 128k and on the skewed eight, in both C runs (they must agree in sign: a C that disagrees with its twin is drift, not an increment). Soft: a stall or a hang here is read against H1-H5 (this profile has no wave-2 lever). Duration (estimate): 130 min.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/w2 eight-seat 262k wave-2 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/w2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/w2 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-w1
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k,concurrent8_code_128k,concurrent8_skew
